From 98ce4a7a80e21c7f7699cbca0e1fb7508f5eedbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:58:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Corrections of the second review of the views

- updateValues: the message of an exception thrown by the operations is
  copied (the error backtrace kept a pointer to the message of a
  destroyed exception).
- Fortran: the tangent operator getters of a material data manager and
  of a behaviour data return the transpose of the tangent operator, of
  shape [gs, ths] at each point (the shape [ths, gs] scrambled the values
  of a non square operator), and refuse a tangent operator which is not a
  single block. C and Fortran getters of the number of values of the
  tangent operator blocks of a material data manager.
- no field view on the values of a temporary function, which owns them.
- OpenMP: one thread per point, without division per value.
- a tangent operator block of a material data manager without point is an
  empty view, as for a material data view.
- the move constructor of RotationMatrix3D, which copies its constant
  axes, is not noexcept; a moved-from material axis must not be used.
- the missing material properties and external state variables are
  reported with the stage of the time step.
- documentation: outputs of a failing point unspecified (integration and
  post-processings, managers and views), synchronization of the field
  operations, fills of the CUDA and HIP operations, use of views in
  device code, release notes.
- tests: tangent operator blocks of a failing point not written, error
  of the operations reported, no allocation by the initialize functions
  and the post-processings (aligned allocations counted), no view on a
  temporary function, non square and refused tangent operators in
  Fortran.
